# CORAS threat diagram: how a threat reaches an asset.
#
# The story reads left to right:
#   threat -> vulnerability -> threat scenario -> unwanted incident -> asset
# The text on an arrow is the likelihood, and on a harm arrow the consequence.

diagram "Threats to the clinical record"

threat        "Curious staff member"                as curious  kind=accidental
threat        "Ransomware"                          as ransom   kind=non-human
threat        "Outside attacker"                    as outsider kind=deliberate

vulnerability "Shared clinical workstation login"   as shared
vulnerability "No offline backup"                   as nobackup
vulnerability "Unpatched VPN gateway"               as vpn

scenario      "Staff member browses records out of curiosity" as browse
scenario      "Files encrypted by ransomware"       as encrypted
scenario      "Attacker reaches the internal network" as inside

incident      "Patient record disclosed to an unauthorised person" as disclosed
incident      "Clinical system unavailable for a day"              as down

asset         "Patient health record"               as ehr
asset         "Availability of the clinical system" as avail

region        "Hospital network"                    as net contains=shared,browse,nobackup,encrypted

curious   -> shared
shared    -> browse     "possible"
browse    -> disclosed  "likely"

ransom    -> nobackup
nobackup  -> encrypted  "unlikely"
encrypted -> down       "certain"

outsider  -> vpn
vpn       -> inside     "possible"
inside    -> browse     "possible"

disclosed -> ehr        "major"
down      -> avail      "catastrophic"
